  "Hand-illustrated cover: “Passeig dels Plataners, Laberint dels Símbols” (the plane-tree walk, labyrinth of symbols), with the labyrinth plan and a key to its symbols: reflexology circles, cross, yin and yang, triskele, choku-rei": "",
  "THE PLANE-TREE WALK": "",
  "<p>The plane-tree walk is a quiet, restful passage between trees, plane trees to be exact, which shelter “the labyrinth of life” in their shade. You can stroll, play, meditate, think, or simply watch, or walk the labyrinth.</p><p>Plane trees are among the species best at absorbing CO₂. They also regulate humidity and temperature, give shade and soften noise.</p><p>Their bark gives the trunk a dappled look in many shades, from grey through ochres and browns, which makes them singular, unmistakable and a little magical.</p><p>It changes with the seasons. In spring and summer the planes are dressed in thick green leaves, giving the walk a green roof that shelters and strokes the labyrinth and the people walking it. In autumn the falling leaves lay a carpet of ochres and browns that hides the labyrinth completely. And in winter the labyrinth is uncovered again, along with the little nests that sparrows, greenfinches, serins and goldfinches built in spring and summer to raise their young.</p><p>At the end of the walk you find a sheltered, welcoming spot. A great mulberry tree casts its shade over a well-hidden little square, surrounded by some unusual places: a tipi, the secret den, and a solar dryer. They are almost magical places that let you feel things quite unlike anything before. A starry night makes them perfect.</p><p><b>The tipi</b> It is hidden under a covering of honeysuckle that makes it feel like nowhere else. Inside you can meditate, chat in a small group, spend a romantic night…</p><p><b>The secret den</b> Tucked beneath an iron dome covered in thick climbing ivy is this hidden refuge. As if you were stepping inside mother earth, it takes you in and protects you, and lets you feel mystery and reflection.</p>": "",
  "(The labyrinth of symbols)": "",
  "Painted plan of the labyrinth of life, with its spirals and symbols": "",
  "<p>The “Labyrinth of life” offers you a path that, as in life, lets you choose. It begins with the Reiki symbol called Choku-rei, and from the first step you decide whether to turn right or left.</p><p>Along the way you meet forks that make you choose: carry straight on, or, if curiosity tempts you, take the turning at each crossroads towards new places, where you will find a series of symbols that will surprise you and tell you a great deal.</p><p>On the way you will also find reflexology circles that invite you to take off your shoes for a foot massage, stimulating the reflex points and making your walk much gentler.</p>": "",
